  "short_description": "Algorithmic Contract Types Unified Standards",
  "long_description": "ACTUS (Algorithmic Contract Types Unified Standards) provides mathematically precise definitions for all financial contract types \u2014 from simple loans (PAM) to complex derivatives. Unlike accounting-focused schemas, ACTUS captures the complete cash flow algorithm for each contract type, enabling deterministic simulation of future cash flows under any market scenario. Widely adopted for stress testing and IRRBB compliance.",
  "when_to_use": "Use for fintech applications modeling loan portfolios, bond analytics, derivative pricing, or regulatory stress testing. EU Solvency II and Basel IV implementations benefit from ACTUS-aligned data models. Essential for any system that needs to calculate future cash flows algorithmically rather than storing static schedules."
}